<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Cuba in Arms</h1><p class="st-meta">1868 CE – 1898 CE</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The insurgent republic proclaimed by Cuban rebels in their wars of independence against Spain, with its own constitutions, presidents and assembly.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 10 October 1868 the planter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-manuel-de-cespedes">Carlos Manuel de Céspedes</a> freed his enslaved workers and proclaimed independence at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-demajagua">La Demajagua</a>, starting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-years-war">Ten Years' War</a>. In April 1869 an assembly at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-guaimaro">Guáimaro</a> adopted a constitution creating the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> in Arms, with Céspedes as president.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic had no fixed capital; its government moved through the eastern countryside held by rebel armies. A legislative House of Representatives often clashed with the president and deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-manuel-de-cespedes">Céspedes</a> in 1873. Generals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximo-gomez">Máximo Gómez</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-maceo">Antonio Maceo</a> led the fighting. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pact-of-zanjon">Pact of Zanjón</a> of 1878 the republic lapsed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-marti">José Martí's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuban-revolutionary-party">Cuban Revolutionary Party</a> relaunched the war in 1895, and new constitutions at Jimaguayú in 1895 and La Yaya in 1897 revived it.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> intervened in 1898 and defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, but excluded the Cuban republic from the peace talks. Its assembly dissolved itself in 1899, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> passed under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/united-states-military-government-in-cuba">United States Military Government in Cuba</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-cuba-in-arms.jpg" alt="Republic of Cuba in Arms" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: HapHaxion · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C%C3%A9spedes_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1868 CE – 1898 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Carlos Manuel de Céspedes, Salvador Cisneros Betancourt, Bartolomé Masó</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/cuba">Cuba</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>República de Cuba en Armas</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1883&amp;focus=republic-of-cuba-in-arms" aria-label="Republic of Cuba in Arms on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2585 1389 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Cuba in Arms lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2801 1580h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2905 1645h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M2905 1645h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Cuba. <a href="/atlas?year=1883&amp;focus=republic-of-cuba-in-arms">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
